All 3 tests pass. The fix: in MSTest 3.8+ (and 4.x), the `out` parameter overload was removed from `Assert.IsInstanceOfType<T>`. Replace:

```csharp
// Old (no longer compiles)
Assert.IsInstanceOfType<T>(value, out var typed);

// New
Assert.IsInstanceOfType<T>(value);
var typed = (T)value;
```

The assertion still validates the type; you just cast afterward since the assert guarantees it won't fail.
